tion_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:c98682b6c1681d0141f50d842c3c731bf44faf17833e7ceec1d21f8ac4709ff4","file":"preprints/Minimal-models-and-Mori-fibre-spaces-for-generalized-log-canonical-Q-pairs-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":16,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e633a21d6e96c887ba8b5da1629a4cb3d905c3dfe29847dc391205dec73721ea","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Minimal-models-and-Mori-fibre-spaces-for-generalized-log-canonical-Q-pairs-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c98682b6c1681d0141f50d842c3c731bf44faf17833e7ceec1d21f8ac4709ff4","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Minimal-models-and-Mori-fibre-spaces-for-generalized-log-canonical-Q-pairs-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L16"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, and let\n$(X,B+M)$ be a projective generalized log canonical $\\Q$-pair. Thus $X$ is\nnormal and integral, $B$ is an effective rational boundary, and $M$ is the\ntrace of a nef rational Cartier divisor on a higher projective birational\nmodel, with $K_X+B+M$ $\\Q$-Cartier.\n\nThere are a normal integral projective variety $Y$ and a birational map\n$\\phi\\colon X\\dashrightarrow Y$ whose inverse contracts no divisors such\nthat, writing $B_Y=\\phi_*B$ and taking $M_Y$ to be the trace of the same\nnef b-divisor, the generalized pair $(Y,B_Y+M_Y)$ is log canonical and\n\\[\n A_{X,B+M}(E)\\le A_{Y,B_Y+M_Y}(E)\n\\]\nfor every prime divisor $E$ over their common function field. The\ninequality is strict for every divisor on $X$ contracted by $\\phi$.\nMore precisely, the following alternatives are determined by $D=K_X+B+M$:\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item if $D$ is pseudo-effective, then $K_Y+B_Y+M_Y$ is nef;\n\\item if $D$ is not pseudo-effective, there is a projective contraction $h\\colon Y\\to T$ to a normal\nprojective variety with connected fibres such that\n\\[\n \\dim T<\\dim Y,\\qquad \\rho(Y/T)=1,\n \\qquad -(K_Y+B_Y+M_Y)\\text{ is ample over }T.\n\\]\n\\end{enumerate}"}
